  m_text: 'Ensure good governance over big corporations by placing a government representative.


    This
    law requires all major corporations to accept a state-appointed representative
    on their board of directors. The representative has voting rights on key decisions
    involving public interest, such as layoffs, environmental compliance, and executive
    pay. Supporters argue it prevents corporate abuse, while critics see it as government
    overreach into the free market.'
